1. Applicant or (his/her designated Agent) logs in the system (Electronic Public Services Portal) personally or assisted by the Reception Officer.

2. Applicant (Agent) fills in the application form, uploads documents, personally or assisted by the Reception Officer.
    In the case when Applicant or (his/her designated Agent):

a) fills in the application form and uploads the documents assisted by the Reception Officer, the Reception Officer will:
-	Receive and dully register the application for issuing the permit and receive the supporting documents presented by the Applicant;
-	Immediately and unconditionally issue the certificate of confirmation according to the sample given in Annex 3 to Law 160 as of 22.07.2011;
-	Send the case (electronic copies of the application form and submitted documents) to the Issuing Authority for review;

The application is returned to the Applicant (Agent) only in the case when it does not contain the information necessary to identify the Applicant.
b) fills in the application form and uploads the documents personally, the system will:
-	automatically generate the document in electronic format confirming the receipt of the application and the set of documents ("the certificate of confirmation") and will;
-	automatically direct the request and the set of documents to the Issuing Authority; 

3. The Issuing Authority (Specialist) opens the case, reviews the application and supporting documents, verifies compliance with the conditions. In case it was found out that not all documents/information required expressly by the legislation were submitted, the Issuing Authority (Specialist) will suspend the examination of the application and will immediately inform the Applicant about the suspension, specifying and describing the grounds for the suspension, the deadline and the remedial actions needed to initiate the examination of the application. 

4. The specialist examines the case and organizes the additional internal examinations necessary to make the decision to issue the authorization. This will require the police in the area where the work will be carried out to undertake an unannounced check to establish the compliance of premises with the technical requirements for the rooms and objects in which narcotic, psychotropic and/or precursor substances will be stored. 

5. The specialist issues the permit or writes a letter of rejection with appropriate justification under the law, with direct notification of the applicant and only if the applicant does not meet the conditions expressly specified in the law or, upon the case, does not demonstrate the fulfillment of these conditions during the suspension period, which will be examined and signed by the director of the issuing authority. Thus, if the control report issued by the police authorities indicates the absence of deviations from the requirements of the legislation, the specialist issues the permit (or writes a letter of rejection in case of deviations from the requirements of the legislation), which will be examined and signed by the Director of the Agency.

6. Once the permit (letter) is issued, the Applicant (Agent) receives an email notification, downloads the permit and confirms the receipt.

7. In case the permit is being issued in hard copy (per Applicant’s request or by the issuing agency’s rules), the Reception Officer prints the permit, delivers it to the Applicant (Agent) and confirms receipt.
